    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1238">

                <pb facs="1096" n="782" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg782"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1261</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgenthau</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi><anchor n="2" xml:id="d1238-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-23T11:00:00+02:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 23, 1914, 11 a.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 26, 11:56 a.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>76. Your telegrams 61, November 21, 7 p.m., and 63, November 21, 5 p.m.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d1238-f2"/> Saw Minister of War and Minister of the Interior
                    together. They state Acaba and Focei unfortified and protected only by few <hi
                        rendition="#italic">gendarmes</hi> performing police duty [who] should not
                    be considered armed forces. If British Government will give assurances that in
                    the future they will not bombard any unfortified port unless they are attacked
                    by armed Ottoman forces, then the Ottoman Government will allow all British
                    subjects to leave Turkey.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
